    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="11" corresp="#wit-d">And ciricsceat gelæste man be Martinus mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And ciricsceat gelæste man be Martinus mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And church dues shall be rendered by Martinmas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And Church dues are to be paid by the Feast of Saint Martin.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Kirchensteuer sei zum Martinusfest entrichtet;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let church-scot be paid by Martinmas;</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="265"><ref target="clause:IIEg_3">II Eg 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_10">I Cn 10</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="29"><label>substantially repeats</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2-2">II Eg 2.2–3</ref> <quote>The references in Wulfstan's codes for Æthelred and Cnut substantially repeated what Edgar had said</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Eg 3.</note>
      </div>
